 61CU c  2013Sc06, 2013ScZZ: E(|a)=38 MeV from WNSL-Yale tandem accelerator     
 61CU2c  facility. Measured triton spectra, |s(|q), spectroscopic               
 61CU3c  factor C{+2}S using a split-pole spectrograph. FWHM |?64 keV.          
 61CU4c  Target=204 |mg/cm{+2} thick, 99.7% enriched. Deduced levels, J, |p.    
 61CU5c  DWBA analysis. Comparison with shell-model calculations.               
 61CU c  The main purpose of the neutron adding and neutron removal reaction    
 61CU2c  studies by 2013Sc06 was to obtain occupancies of neutron orbitals,     
 61CU3c  proton vacancies, and energy centroids of neutron, neutron-holes,      
 61CU4c  proton-single particle excitations in {+60}Ni and {+62}Ni, and thereby 
 61CU5c  investigate closure of 0f{-7/2} shell. Some data details of this study 
 61CU6c  are supplied in 2013ScZZ                                               
 61CU c  1967Ar05: E(|a)=26.7 MeV. Measured |s(|q), |q(c.m.)=11|'-48|'.|DE-E    
 61CU2c  semi telescope with FWHM|?90 keV. Enriched target. Three groups are    
 61CU3c  reported at 0, 470 and 970 keV                                         
 61CU c  L-values and spectroscopic factors are from comparisons with DWBA      
 61CU2c  calculations with a DWBA normalization factor of 38.4.                 
